.TH OAIOAUTHC 1 "July 2026" "oaioauthc 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oaioauthc \- expose a ChatGPT OAuth session through a local
OpenAI-compatible API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oaioauthc serve
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR host ]
.RB [ \-\-models
.IR ids ]
.RB [ \-\-codex-version
.IR version ]
.RB [ \-\-base-url
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-\-oauth-file
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-oauth-client-id
.IR id ]
.RB [ \-\-oauth-token-url
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-\-daemon ]
.RB [ \-\-runtime-dir
.IR directory ]
.RB [ \-\-debug-json [ =compact | =pretty ]]
.PP
.B oaioauthc login
.RB [ \-\-device-auth ]
.RB [ \-\-oauth-file
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-oauth-issuer
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-\-oauth-client-id
.IR id ]
.RB [ \-\-oauth-token-url
.IR url ]
.RB [ \-\-open | \-\-no-open ]
.RB [ \-\-login-timeout-ms
.IR milliseconds ]
.PP
.B oaioauthc status
.RB [ \-\-runtime-dir
.IR directory ]
.PP
.B oaioauthc stop
.RB [ \-\-runtime-dir
.IR directory ]
.PP
.B oaioauthc logs
.RB [ \-\-follow ]
.RB [ \-\-runtime-dir
.IR directory ]
.PP
.B oaioauthc
.RB [ \-\-help | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oaioauthc
uses a ChatGPT OAuth session to serve a local subset of the OpenAI HTTP API.
It supports model discovery, Responses, Chat Completions, image generation,
and image editing.
.PP
The proxy is stateless: it does not store response objects or conversation
history.  Clients must send the complete conversation with each request.
.PP
With no command, or when the first argument is an option,
.B serve
is selected.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B serve
Listen for local OpenAI-compatible HTTP requests.  The default address is
127.0.0.1 and the default port is 10531.  The process continues until it
receives a terminating signal or encounters a fatal listener error.
.TP
.B login
Perform an OAuth PKCE login using a callback listener on localhost port 1455.
The callback wait is limited to five minutes by default.  Existing credentials
are replaced only after confirmation from an interactive terminal.  With
.B \-\-device-auth ,
print a verification URL and one-time code, then poll for approval on another
device; no callback listener or browser is used.  Device login waits up to 15
minutes by default.
.TP
.B status
Query the live daemon control socket and print its JSON status.  A stale
metadata file without a responding control socket is not considered running.
.TP
.B stop
Request graceful daemon shutdown and return success only after its control
socket disappears.
.TP
.B logs
Copy the daemon log to standard output.  With
.B \-\-follow
continue reading appended data until the daemon stops.
.SH SERVE OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p " " \fIport\fR ", " \-\-port " " \fIport\fR
Listen on the specified decimal TCP port.  Valid values are 1 through 65535.
The default is 10531.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " host"
Bind to the specified host or address.  The default is 127.0.0.1.
Values other than 127.0.0.1, localhost, and ::1 cause an exposure warning.
The proxy does not authenticate incoming clients.
.TP
.BI \-\-models " ids"
Expose the exact comma-separated model IDs instead of discovering the account
catalog.  Empty entries are ignored.  Requests still must select a non-empty
model explicitly.
.TP
.BI \-\-codex-version " version"
Use the specified Codex client version for upstream requests instead of
discovering the current version from the Codex package registry.
.TP
.BI \-\-base-url " url"
Use the specified Codex upstream root URL.  Endpoint suffixes such as
responses and models are appended to this value.  The URL must use HTTPS.
HTTP is permitted only for explicit loopback endpoints (localhost, 127.0.0.1,
or [::1]) used during local testing.
.TP
.BI \-\-debug-json
Write parsed client JSON and normalized upstream JSON to standard error in
compact form.
.TP
.BI \-\-debug-json=compact
Select compact diagnostic JSON explicitly.
.TP
.BI \-\-debug-json=pretty
Select indented diagnostic JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Detach the
.B serve
command into a session independent of the invoking terminal.  Startup does
not return until the listener has successfully bound.  Standard output and
standard error are appended to the daemon log.
.TP
.BI \-\-runtime-dir " directory"
Use the specified private runtime directory for daemon lock, metadata,
control socket, and log files.  The default is
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/oaioauthc ,
then
.IR $HOME/.local/state/oaioauthc ,
then
.IR ./.local/state/oaioauthc .
The directory and regular runtime files are created with modes 0700 and 0600.
.PP
Diagnostic JSON redacts OAuth token fields, encrypted reasoning content, and
image data URLs.  It does not redact prompts, conversation history, or tool
definitions.
.SH LOGIN OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-device-auth
Use the headless device authorization flow.  The command prints a short-lived
user code and verification URL, then waits for the user to approve the request
on a trusted device.  This option cannot be combined with
.B \-\-open
or
.BR \-\-no-open .
Device authorization is a beta OpenAI feature and may need to be enabled in
ChatGPT security or workspace settings.  Enter the code only after starting
the login yourself; a code supplied by a website or another person may be a
phishing attempt.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Request the system desktop opener after printing the authorization URL.
This is the default.  Browser launch failure does not fail the login command.
.TP
.B \-\-no-open
Do not start a browser.  The authorization URL is still printed to standard
error.
.TP
.BI \-\-login-timeout-ms " milliseconds"
Set the overall login timeout in milliseconds.  For browser login this covers
the callback and callback-request waits; for device login it covers code
request, polling, and the final token exchange.  The value must be a positive
decimal integer no greater than the largest signed integer supported by the
build.  The default is 300000 for browser login and 900000 for device login.
.SH COMMON OAUTH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-oauth-issuer " url"
Set the OpenAI OAuth issuer root used to construct authorization, device, and
default token endpoints.  The default is
.BR https://auth.openai.com .
This login-only option is useful with a compatible private issuer; use
.B \-\-oauth-token-url
when only the final token endpoint differs.  The issuer must use HTTPS, except
that HTTP is permitted only for explicit loopback endpoints (localhost,
127.0.0.1, or [::1]) used during local testing.
.TP
.BI \-\-oauth-file " path"
Read or write credentials at the specified path instead of the default
auth.json path.
.TP
.BI \-\-oauth-client-id " id"
Override the OAuth client ID used for login and token refresh.  This advanced
option is accepted by both
.B login
and
.BR serve .
.TP
.BI \-\-oauth-token-url " url"
Override the endpoint that receives authorization codes and refresh tokens.
This advanced option is accepted by both commands.  Credentials are sent to
the specified URL.  It must use HTTPS, except that HTTP is permitted only for
explicit loopback endpoints (localhost, 127.0.0.1, or [::1]) used during local
testing.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CODEX_HOME
When non-empty, the default credential path is
.IR $CODEX_HOME/auth.json .
.TP
.B HOME
When
.B CODEX_HOME
is unset or empty, the default credential path is
.IR $HOME/.codex/auth.json .
If both variables are unavailable, the fallback is
.IR ./.codex/auth.json .
.TP
.B BROWSER
With
.BR \-\-open ,
use this value as the browser executable when it is non-empty and contains no
whitespace.  The value is executed directly, without a shell.  The default is
.B open
on macOS and
.B xdg-open
on other systems.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $CODEX_HOME/auth.json
Preferred default credential file when
.B CODEX_HOME
is set.
.TP
.I $HOME/.codex/auth.json
Default credential file otherwise.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/oaioauthc/runtime.lock
Stable advisory lock held by a detached daemon.  It remains after shutdown
so its inode can safely be reused by a later start.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/oaioauthc/runtime.json
Atomic informational metadata for the live daemon.  Status uses the control
socket as the source of truth and removes this file during shutdown.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/oaioauthc/control.sock
Private AF_UNIX control socket accepting the bounded
.BR STATUS
and
.BR STOP
commands.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/oaioauthc/server.log
Append-only daemon standard-output and standard-error log.  It is retained
after shutdown for inspection.
.PP
New credential files are written with mode 0600 through a synchronized
temporary file and atomic installation.  Refresh operations use a sibling
.I .lock
file to serialize credential rotation.
.SH HTTP INTERFACE
The default API root is
.IR http://127.0.0.1:10531/v1 .
The supported routes and request limitations are documented in
.IR docs/api-compatibility.md
in the source distribution.
.PP
The health endpoint is available at
.I /health
and does not load OAuth credentials.  Every
.I /v1
route requires a usable saved OAuth session.  Incoming Authorization headers
are not used for local client authentication.
.SH SECURITY
Keep the listener on a loopback address.  Binding to a network-visible address
allows other hosts to use the saved ChatGPT OAuth session because the proxy has
no inbound authentication layer.
.PP
Upstream connections require TLS 1.2 or newer.  Custom Codex and OAuth URLs
must use HTTPS, except for explicit loopback HTTP endpoints used in local
testing.
.PP
Treat auth.json and its tokens as passwords.  Enable diagnostic JSON only when
needed, and protect standard-error logs because prompts and conversation
content remain visible.
.PP
The daemon control socket is protected by the private runtime directory and
socket mode 0600.  It is a local administrative interface, not an HTTP
endpoint and not a substitute for inbound API authentication.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful option display, a completed login, or a login
cancelled at the credential-overwrite prompt.  A non-zero status indicates
invalid command-line input, login failure, or fatal server setup or listener
failure.  Signal termination status is determined by the invoking shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
Log in without starting a browser:
.PP
.nf
oaioauthc login --no-open
.fi
.PP
Serve on the default loopback address:
.PP
.nf
oaioauthc serve
.fi
.PP
Discover available model IDs:
.PP
.nf
curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:10531/v1/models
.fi
.PP
Send a Responses request:
.PP
.nf
curl -sS http://127.0.0.1:10531/v1/responses \e
    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \e
    -d '{"model":"MODEL_ID","input":"Say hello."}'
.fi
.PP
Start a detached local daemon and inspect or stop it:
.PP
.nf
oaioauthc serve --daemon
oaioauthc status
oaioauthc logs --follow
oaioauthc stop
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1)
